course: dictionary
lesson: 2757
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can find which meaning the writer means by reading the context: the words and sentences around the word. «You are about a centimetre taller in the morning than at bedtime, because the soft discs between the bones of your back squash a little during the day.» Bones and back are the clues, so disc here means a pad inside your spine.
explain: Now read «The Milky Way is our galaxy, a huge disc of a few hundred billion stars.» Here a disc is a large, flat, round shape, not something you hold. The clues are huge and galaxy. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes a whole phrase gives the meaning. A flying disc is something you throw in PE, and a compact disc stores music. The same word can change meaning, so read the rest of the sentence before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Disc» means a flat, thin, round object.
fact: «Disc» can also mean a round, flat object that stores music, films or computer data, such as a CD or DVD.
fact: «Disc» can mean one of the small pads of tough material between the bones of your spine.
fact: «Disc» is spelled «disk» in American English.
exercise: «A drinks can starts as a flat disc of aluminium punched into a cup and stretched tall.» In this sentence, what is a disc? | A small pad of tough material in your spine | A film stored for watching at home | A flying toy for PE | *A flat, thin, round piece of metal
exercise: Ella says, «The Milky Way is a huge disc of stars.» Which meaning of disc fits here? | *A large, flat, round shape | A CD or DVD for storing films | A pad between the bones of your back | A toy to throw in the park
exercise: «Alessandro Volta made the first battery from a pile of metal discs and cloth soaked in salty water.» What are the discs in this sentence? | Computer data stores | *Flat, thin, round pieces of metal | Round toys for playing outside | Pads of tough material in your spine
test: «Each day the soft discs between your bones squash a little, so you are taller in the morning.» What does disc mean here? | A round object for playing games | *A pad of tough material between the bones of your spine | A flat round shape in space | A shiny CD for music
test: Mia says, «Put the disc in the player to watch the film.» Which meaning fits best? | A flying toy used in PE | A flat, round piece of metal | *A round, flat object that stores films | A pad in your back
exam: Jayden asks, «What does disc mean?» Which answer uses context best? | Disc only ever means a pad in your spine | Disc always means a frisbee | *It depends on the sentence: read the words around it to find the meaning | A disc is always a CD
